<title>POLAND: Kable surges on NKT Cables tender.</title>
<headline>Kable surges on NKT Cables tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish cable maker Kable SA, whose trade had been suspended on Tuesday, surged 10 percent to 45.1 zlotys after 50-percent owner NKT Cables on Monday called a public tender offer, traders said.</p>
<p>The Danish firm offered to buy Kable's remaining one million shares at the then market price of 41 zlotys.</p>
<p>The stock did not trade after price fixing due to excess demand, which traders said signalled another rise on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
